# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore — files Docker hides from `COPY` during image builds.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES:
# When the Dockerfile runs `COPY app ./app` or `COPY pyproject.toml ./`,
# Docker first sends the "build context" (the folder containing the
# Dockerfile + everything in it) to the Docker daemon. Without this
# file, that context includes .git/, .venv/, __pycache__/, the docs
# folder, secrets, and editor crud — easily hundreds of MB of stuff
# the image doesn't need.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS:
#   - Smaller build context = faster builds (less data to ship)
#   - Smaller image = faster pulls onto rishi-4/5/6
#   - Prevents accidents: a stray .env.local NEVER ends up in the image
#   - Cache-friendly: changes to .git/ don't bust the COPY layer
#
# RELATED FILES (footer at the end).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Version control --------------------------------------------------------
# The .git directory is huge and the running service never needs it.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Python build + cache artifacts ----------------------------------------
# These are produced by running tests or installing locally. The Dockerfile
# does its own clean install inside the builder stage, so the host's
# leftovers would only confuse it (or worse, copy in incompatible wheels
# built for a different libc).
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info
.eggs
build
dist
.venv
venv
env
.pytest_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.tox
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# --- Editor / IDE crud ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# --- Local secrets and runtime config --------------------------------------
# Per CONSTRAINTS D8, .env.local is gitignored and holds developer secrets
# (Postgres password for local Compose, etc.). It MUST never end up in the
# production image — runtime secrets come from Swarm secrets, not the image.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Docs, planning, and dev-only folders ----------------------------------
# Docs are read on GitHub or via `git clone`, not from inside the container.
# Tests run in CI against the source repo, not against the prod image.
docs
tests
*.md
!README.md

# --- Docker compose files --------------------------------------------------
# Compose files orchestrate containers from the OUTSIDE; the running image
# never needs to read them. Excluding them keeps the image cleaner.
#
# We deliberately do NOT exclude Dockerfile / .dockerignore themselves —
# some Docker builders (legacy builder, certain CI setups) need them
# present in the context to bootstrap the build correctly. The cost
# (a few KB inside the build context) is trivial.
docker-compose*.yml


# ===========================================================================
# RELATED FILES:
#   Dockerfile        — the file whose COPY commands this filter affects
#   .gitignore        — the host-side analogue (what git sees vs. what
#                       Docker sees can diverge; keep both consistent)
# ===========================================================================
